weave-knee trial v1
fanout: 8
seed: 1
weaver: claude-sonnet-5
judge: claude-sonnet-5
quality: 2
narrative:
  At the center of Nexdor sits Gridor, the cache: it retries a failed handoff at most twice before parking it, acts only once four of its peers countersign, and refuses new writes while its own sweep is running. Gridor's overflow does not vanish — it delegates that overflow onward to Pamgri, the registry, which answers every read from its newest snapshot only, evicts anything left unclaimed after five ticks, and itself acts only once four of its peers countersign. What Pamgri settles into a sealed ledger, it hands to Kelhul, the courier. Kelhul evicts anything left unclaimed after eleven ticks, retries a failed handoff at most twice before parking it, and keeps only digests of what it carries, never the bodies. When the load Kelhul carries strains, it signals backpressure onward to Pamsax, the monitor. Pamsax evicts anything left unclaimed after ten ticks, keeps digests rather than bodies, and answers reads from its newest snapshot only — the same read discipline Pamgri holds. Pamsax in turn reports missed heartbeats to Dorgri, the gate. Dorgri evicts anything left unclaimed after nine ticks, refuses new writes while its own sweep is running, and retries a failed handoff up to four times before parking it — the most patient retrier in the chain. What Dorgri evicts, it streams onward to Dortol, the vault. Dortol keeps digests, never bodies, acts only once four of its peers countersign, and answers reads from its newest snapshot only. Dortol publishes its sweep verdicts to Nexfel, the beacon. Nexfel acts only once four of its peers countersign, refuses new writes during its own sweep, and answers reads from its newest snapshot only — mirroring Dortol's discipline exactly. Nexfel's overflow is delegated onward to Gritol, the relay. Gritol keeps digests, never bodies, answers reads from its newest snapshot only, and retries a failed handoff up to three times before parking it. Gritol closes the circuit: it hands its sealed ledger back to Gridor, completing a ring that runs cache to registry to courier to monitor to gate to vault to beacon to relay and back to cache again.

  Two overflow paths sit on this same ring rather than a separate one: Gridor's overflow into Pamgri opens the loop, and Nexfel's overflow into Gritol closes it, so the system sheds excess load at two points on one circuit rather than draining to somewhere outside it. Four of the eight modules — Gridor, Pamgri, Dortol, and Nexfel — will not act until four peers countersign, spacing that quorum discipline at four separate stations around the ring instead of concentrating it at one checkpoint. Four modules — Kelhul, Pamsax, Dortol, and Gritol — keep only digests of what passes through them, so full bodies persist only at Gridor, Pamgri, Dorgri, and Nexfel. Eviction windows differ unevenly as data moves around the ring: five ticks at Pamgri, eleven at Kelhul, ten at Pamsax, nine at Dorgri, while Gridor, Dortol, and Nexfel are not stated to evict at all. Retries also vary by station: two attempts at Gridor and at Kelhul, three at Gritol, four at Dorgri, while Pamgri, Pamsax, Dortol, and Nexfel are not stated to retry a handoff. Sweeps that refuse new writes occur at three points on the ring — Gridor, Dorgri, and Nexfel — so the system has three places where it can go temporarily closed to incoming writes while it settles itself, spaced roughly a third of the way apart around the same loop that carries the ledger from Gritol back to Gridor.
